## The ADCS's mass, power and volume budget of a product, transcribed from adcs-design lib.rs (budget) and the twin's
## asils.product.load budget_: each fill line counts its units (the axes, spin axes, boresights or normals it lists, the
## last of them it lists; the coarse Sun sensors are one unit however many normals; one when it lists none), and each
## unit takes its part's mass, steady power (else its power, else its power at the full dipole) and volume, none when the
## part states none. The totals are gb_0 (mass), gb_1 (orbit-average power) and gb_3 (volume); gb_2, the peak power, is
## not computed by the sizing: the steady sum stands for it (a finding for design). Masses in kg, powers in W, volumes
## in L: plain numbers.
## The developer's transcription (S7.15), unsigned.
module sizebudget

## A product's fill slot (adcs-product/1): the coils, wheels, fluid rings, CMGs, VSCMGs, thrusters, the star tracker, the
## magnetometer, the fine Sun sensors, the gyro, the GNSS receiver, the Earth sensor, the coarse Sun sensors, any other.
choice Slot = coils, wheels, rings, cmg, vscmg, rcs, star_tracker, magnetometer, sun_sensors, gyro, gnss, earth_sensor, \
              coarse_sun_sensors, other

## One fill line of slot s: how many units (from the lengths of the axes, spin axes, boresights and normals it lists, -1
## where it lists none), and their mass, power and volume from the part's mass, steady power ps, power pw, power at the
## full dipole pm and volume (nan where the part states none).
fn budget_line(s: Slot, na: int in -1 .. 4, ns: int in -1 .. 4, nb: int in -1 .. 2, nn: int in -1 .. 6, mass: real[1] in 0 .. 2, \
               ps: real[1] in 0 .. 10, pw: real[1] in 0 .. 10, pm: real[1] in 0 .. 10, vol: real[1] in 0 .. 2) \
        -> (n: real[1], m: real[1], p: real[1], v: real[1])
    n = 1.0
    let counts = [na, ns, nb, nn]
    for i in 0 .. 4
        if counts[i] >= 0
            n = real(counts[i])
            if s == Slot.coarse_sun_sensors
                n = 1.0
            end
        end
    end
    let mm = if isnan(mass) then 0.0 else mass
    let pp: real[1] = 0.0
    if not isnan(ps)
        pp = ps
    elif not isnan(pw)
        pp = pw
    elif not isnan(pm)
        pp = pm
    end
    let vv = if isnan(vol) then 0.0 else vol
    m = n*mm
    p = n*pp
    v = n*vv
end

## The product's totals over its k lines (each line's mass m, power p, volume v): the ADCS's mass (gb_0), power (gb_1;
## gb_2's stand-in) and volume (gb_3), summed in the fill's order from zero.
## length: 16
fn budget_total(m: inout real[1][*] in 0 .. 2, p: inout real[1][*] in 0 .. 10, v: inout real[1][*] in 0 .. 2, k: int in 0 .. 16) \
        -> (mass: real[1], power: real[1], volume: real[1])
    mass = 0.0
    power = 0.0
    volume = 0.0
    for i in 0 .. k
        mass = mass + m[i]
        power = power + p[i]
        volume = volume + v[i]
    end
end
